18:## Public read boundary
20:The browser uses a same-origin `GET /api/quote-content/v1/:country/form` routed to Strapi through the static app host. Keep Strapi's ordinary Content API authorization enabled and grant the Public role the single custom `api::quote-content.quote-content.readForm` action. Enable neither generated CRUD routes for these content types nor public draft, preview, plugin, search, media, or admin actions. The frontend sends no authorization token. The static host proxies the dedicated read path only and returns no substitute SPA HTML for unmatched API paths. Admin access is a separate local binding and uses Strapi admin authentication for editorial access. [Strapi routing](https://docs.strapi.io/cms/backend-customization/routes), [Users & Permissions](https://docs.strapi.io/cms/features/users-permissions)
22:The controller takes the canonical country path parameter and no caller-controlled filters, locale, population, or publication selectors. It explicitly queries published data, populates only the known components, validates the whole content projection, and maps an allowlisted DTO. Success is `200` with `{ schemaVersion: 1, country, fields }` (see [ADR-002](ADR-002-dynamic-form-contract.md)). Public outcomes are `400 INVALID_REQUEST` for unsupported query inputs, `404 UNSUPPORTED_COUNTRY` for an unsupported API path code, `404 FORM_NOT_PUBLISHED` for no published document, `503 FORM_UNAVAILABLE` for configuration invalidity or duplicate documents, and `503 CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE` for CMS retrieval failure. A published document with no fields is invalid. Use a stable `{ error: { code } }` response without stack traces, internal IDs, or raw data. Use `Cache-Control: no-store` on these responses and bypass intermediary cache for this API path. The frontend still decodes success bodies and rejects country or version mismatches. Errors use local accessible fallback copy and retry. Future plan and terms routes require separate public actions after those stories' approvals.
34:The custom route and decoder are deliberate maintenance costs. Editors can publish changes within the supported versioned vocabulary. New field primitives and incompatible contract changes are engineering changes. Confirm exact Public action registration and route permissions in the pinned Strapi version during implementation before exposing the route. Verify both canonical URLs after a hard reload, draft exclusion, rejection of cross-country responses and query overrides, denial of anonymous writes and generated reads, and published change pickup without rebuilding Angular. Trace to AC-US01-01, 05, 08, 09, 11 and 13 and T-US01-01, 06, 08, 09, 11 and 13.

