README.md:44:- The public app uses the same-origin GET paths `/api/quote-content/v1/:country/form` and `/api/quote-content/v1/:country/plans`. The Strapi Public role has only `readForm` and `readPlans` under `api::quote-content.quote-content`. The static host proxies these two reads. The public frontend uses no API token.
docs/adr/ADR-004-plan-catalog-and-selection.md:30:Reuse `{ error: { code } }` and `Cache-Control: no-store` for handler outcomes. Add only `api::quote-content.quote-content.readPlans` to the Public allowlist alongside `readForm`. Extend the exact same-origin proxy allowlist to the plans read path. Keep generated Plan CRUD, previews, raw CMS data and write credentials out of public access. Add fictitious startup plans for both countries using an independent, retry-safe seed that preserves editor changes and deliberate unpublication on later starts.
docs/adr/ADR-005-country-terms-and-simulated-payment.md:11:[ADR-001](ADR-001-multi-country-content.md) reserves a country-scoped terms document and public read action. [ADR-002](ADR-002-dynamic-form-contract.md) establishes the shared runtime decoder pattern. [ADR-003](ADR-003-frontend-quote-state.md) keeps quote state and payment in the browser, and [ADR-004](ADR-004-plan-catalog-and-selection.md) already gates editable Summary on valid Details and a freshly revalidated plan. The existing Angular 21.2 wizard has the Summary handoff and the Strapi 5.63 controller already serves Form and Plans through the same-origin proxy. US-03 needs a terms revision contract, a payment attempt that refreshes consent before it starts, and a terminal receipt that survives reload.
docs/adr/ADR-005-country-terms-and-simulated-payment.md:29:Reuse the `{ error: { code } }` envelope and `Cache-Control: no-store` on handler outcomes. Extend the same-origin, GET-only proxy allowlist and add only `api::quote-content.quote-content.readTerms` to the Public role alongside Form and Plans. Generated CRUD, draft and admin access, and write credentials stay outside the public contract. The terms request carries the country in the path and no quote, consent or payment data. The proxy bypasses caching as it does for Form and Plans. [HTTP caching](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html)

